 3. 🏖️ Scoop: &quot;Delusional&quot; forecast rattles Senate retreat 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Lindsey Bailey/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A pollster for Senate Republicans, Erik Iverson, was met with disbelief yesterday after he told GOP donors and operatives that they can add seats in November's midterm elections, sources tell Axios' Stef W. Kight. 

 In fact, Republicans are increasingly fearful they'll lose their majority. "Delusional," an attendee at a National Republican Senatorial Committee retreat in Sea Island, Ga., told Axios after the presentation.

 "The mood is not good," griped another. "I think most attendees down here are politically astute and realistic about the headwinds Republicans face," said a third. 🗳️ Zoom in: The NRSC's Sea Island fall retreat is a major donor event that attracts big-dollar givers, senators and their senior staff.

 Iverson, a former Montana Republican Party chair, suggested Republicans could gain one seat in the Senate after the midterms, but didn't provide a state-by-state explanation. Iverson told Axios that he "pointed out  that in 2022 President Biden's image was double digits underwater in every single swing Senate seat, yet Democrats still gained a seat. The message was for folks to keep their heads up."

