 6. 🍲 World&#x27;s busiest restaurant 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Cooks in the kitchen at Aga's Restaurant in Houston in 2023. Photo: Jon Shapley/Houston Chronicle via Getty Images Aga's — an unassuming, family-run Indian-Pakistani joint in a Houston strip mall — is one of the world's most popular restaurants.

 Aga's serves about 4,000 people and packs about 1,600 takeout orders every day, N.Y. Times food reporter Priya Krishna writes . Uber Eats says it delivers more to-go orders from Aga's than any other restaurant in the world. Many Uber Eats drivers in the area say they only deliver Aga's. 😋 The secret sauce: Aga's is beloved for its menu of regional favorites from India and Pakistan. 

 Aga's mastered delivery before 2020, positioning it to thrive during the pandemic. Now, the restaurant's old storage room is a dedicated call center to field the flood of incoming takeout orders. The intrigue: The volume of orders gives Aga's "distinct leverage over delivery companies, which restaurateurs typically loathe for their hefty fees," The Times says. 

 One of the owners "said he was able to persuade DoorDash, Uber Eats and Grubhub to lower their commissions in exchange for the restaurant's business." Read on (gift link). 

 
 
