 8. 🍽️ 1 for the road: Meet your neighbors 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Maura Losch/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 More than 1,200 Axios readers coast to coast have signed up for dinner with people they've never met on Oct. 6.

 It's part of Axios Social Club, an experiment Axios Local has been running in partnership with the DNNR dinner-club platform. Readers take a personality quiz and get matched with five other locals for dinner. We pick the restaurants: You don't find out where you're going until event day. 💡 It's a signal of a broader yearning for human connection , Axios Local's Emma Way tells us: 

 Making friends as an adult is hard, loneliness is real, and people are hungry for reasons to get off their phones and connect IRL. 📨 Want to get dinner with your neighbors? Book your seat for our Axios Social Club dinner on Tuesday, Oct. 6, in one of 41 Axios Local cities. 

 
 
